Modified in November 2026 from Luma Palette for Clip Studio Paint v0.1.3.
Changes include pen contact-drag selection, Japanese localization, additional
color pickers, configurable palette and eyedropper shortcuts, pinned position
persistence, and changes to CSP color synchronization. This public repository starts with an independent initial commit; earlier private development history is not included.

The corresponding-source archive accompanying the Windows portable build
contains the application source and the locked Windows x64 Rust dependency
packages, with their original notices and a license inventory. The Mozilla
Public License 2.0 applies to the identified MPL dependencies and is available
at https://www.mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.

The canvas weave texture at src/assets/canvas-weave-prototype.png and
fine-art-paper texture at src/assets/fine-art-paper.png are procedurally
generated assets. Their generators are provided in scripts/. Canvas weaving
uses optional Python regeneration dependencies; fine-art paper uses the Python
standard library only. Neither generator is an application runtime dependency.
